-- title:
--   Stable line at λ ∥ M with a_λ = ± 1
-- statement:
--   Let $M \geq 1$ and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ that is a newform in the project's sense: $g$ is a normalised eigenform (first $q$-coefficient $1$, coefficients multiplicative on coprime indices, and the two recursions at primes prime to $M$ and at primes dividing $M$) and for no proper divisor of $M$ does there exist a normalised eigenform of weight two and that level agreeing with $g$ in all coefficients at primes not dividing $M$. Let $\lambda$ be prime, and $S$ a finite set of naturals with $\lambda \in S$ and containing every prime divisor of $M$. Let $O'$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathbb{C}$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 (S \ {lam})`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the space of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S \setminus \{\lambda\}$, together with $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$, $q \notin S \setminus \{\lambda\}$, and assume $\chi_g(T_\ell) = a_\ell(g)$ for all such $\ell$. Let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the image of $\chi_g$ into $O'$. Assume $\lambda \mid M$, $\lambda^2 \nmid M$, and $\chi_g(U_\lambda) = a_\lambda(g)$ (note $U_\lambda$ is among the generators, since $\lambda \notin S \setminus \{\lambda\}$). Finally let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $\lambda$, i.e. with $\lambda$ a non-unit of $P$. Then there is a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain $O''$ with finite residue field, an $O'$-algebra that is module-finite over $O'$ with injective local structure map, and a two-dimensional $\lambda$-adically continuous representation $\rho$ of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ on a free $O''$-module $V$ of rank two (an element of [`GaloisRepAdic O''`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16)) with the following two properties. First, for every prime $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $\ell$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ acting on the residue field by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))X + \ell$, the coefficient being taken in $O''$ via $O' \to O''$. Second, there are an $O''$-submodule $L \subseteq V$ and an integer $a \in \{1,-1\}$ with $a_\lambda(g) = a$ in $\mathbb{C}$, such that $L = O'' \cdot b_0$ for some $O''$-basis $(b_0,b_1)$ of $V$, $L$ is stable under $\rho(\sigma)$ for all $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, every element of the inertia subgroup of $P$ (taken as a subgroup of the full Galois group) acts trivially modulo $L$, i.e. $\rho(\tau)v - v \in L$ for all $v \in V$, and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\lambda$ for $P$ satisfies $\rho(\sigma)v - a\,v \in L$ for all $v \in V$.
--
--   This is the local description at $\lambda$ of the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to a weight-two newform of level exactly divisible by $\lambda$, in the case where $\lambda$ is also the residue characteristic of the coefficient ring: the multiplicative reduction of $J_0(M)$ at $\lambda$ in the sense of Deligne–Rapoport produces a Galois-stable line $L$ with unramified quotient on which Frobenius acts by the $U_\lambda$-eigenvalue $a_\lambda(g) = \pm 1$, while the characteristic polynomials of Frobenius outside $S$ record the Hecke eigenvalues. It feeds the constructions of $\lambda$-adic representations with a prescribed stable line used in the level-lowering and deformation-theoretic steps at primes exactly dividing the level.
